A:

Here's another way that avoids complex divisions. If the input string is not one of the words, the output is just "not ok". It only works because the word list is alphabetized and we can pre-sort the words by the ASCII value of their letter, so that the - and _ are separate words (just as is the case in the OP's answer).

My approach was to convert the string of characters to a number, and then to use HashMap<Character, Integer> to convert the number back to character and loop through it to figure out the answer. But I don't think it is efficient. Is there any better way to find the desired output?

